{
  "name": "What to Do About Water Damage in Your Mobile Home",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Water damage in a mobile home can feel like a real nightmare, but tackling it quickly is key to minimizing the impact. First things first, you've got to find and stop the source of the water. Whether it's a leaky pipe, a roof issue, or a window seal that's given up, don't patch anything until the leak is completely under control. Leaving wet flooring or wall material in place just invites more problems like mold or further structural weakening, and that can spread beyond the visible area pretty fast. Once the leak is stopped, you need to remove all the damaged material. This isn't just about what you can see; water can seep into insulation, subflooring, and framing, so a thorough assessment is crucial. Trying to fix complex water damage yourself, especially if it involves electrical or plumbing, can lead to bigger, more expensive mistakes. If you're unsure about the extent of the damage or how to fix the underlying cause, don't hesitate to reach out to a professional. HH Remodeling LLC has the experience to assess and repair these kinds of issues, making sure your home is safe and sound.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
